    "title": "Write a practical message",
    "subtitle": "A shared meal · 1",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to choose a meal that meets different preferences and explain the final choice.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U3-05-required-composition-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Compose a purposeful message",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U3-05-required-composition-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "written",
            "prompt": "A shared meal · 1: Write a practical explanation for someone joining the situation late. State the problem, a supported reason or constraint, and a clear proposed next step.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "我和朋友到饭店吃午饭。菜单上有包子、面条儿和米饭。朋友想吃面条儿，我想吃米饭，我们还想先买两个包子，一人吃一个。\n\n包子来了，我吃完一个，觉得还想再吃。朋友只吃了一半，我以为他不喜欢，他说不是，想等面条儿来，吃太多包子就不想再吃面条儿了。\n\n我说，那我再买一个，你不用和我一样。朋友说好。面条儿和米饭来了，我们吃自己想吃的，不因为朋友多吃就多买。\n\n朋友吃完面条儿，又把半个包子吃了。我吃了米饭和两个包子，也不想再买吃的。我们吃的东西不一样，吃的多少也不一样。\n\n走出饭店，朋友说下次先看自己想吃什么，不用一看我买两个就也买两个。我说可以先买一点儿，吃了还想吃，就再买，总比买了又吃不完好。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Write your own message",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed writing practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "The problem, constraint and next step connect coherently."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I distinguished the source facts from my proposal."
              }
            ],
            "minLength": 1
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
